            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cheryle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this recipe. I added kalmata olives &amp; forgot the mint my first attempt, delish! My second try I'm using taboule in place of couscous.",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-31T19:02:53.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angelika"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wwoooooh! Yes, this is a KICK in the mouth if you follow the recipe to a T! However, I still really enjoyed it. It may have been too much for my husband. We used Israeli pearl couscous, as that's what we had on hand, and since we only had 1c of it, I halved all of the other ingredients to match. I made the recipe without deviation, and due to the spice level after mixing it all up, I made the choice to add .. 1/2 cup?? ... Of greek yogurt to help cool it down. It's really good this way, but I do look forward to trying this recipe again, and halving (or more) the cayenne pepper. I would like to try this without the creamy calories added ;-) All in all, I think it's quite fresh and tasty, just need to be mindful of your audience as far as spice level goes.. Adjust accordingly!",
            "datePublished": "2022-06-23T17:40:35.390Z"
          },
          {
